Looking at this problem, I need to determine for which $n$ there exists a continuous map $\omega: \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n$ with a two-sided identity $e \neq 0$ and no zero divisors.

**Answer check:** The problem text contains no leaked answers or solution sketches. Proceeding to solve.

